{"agentDecisions":{"entries":[{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** Which recorded data feed the per-finding and per-reviewer\n  fields?\n- **Answer:** Everything is already in the run journal and result objects:\n  each review result carries `findings` (severity, classId, classStatement,\n  criterion, path, blocking), `unavailableReason`, `rejectionRule`,\n  `normalized`, `reviewerLaunched`; its prepared input carries `roundPolicy`\n  (scope, round, band, regressionPaths); `ROUND_COUNTED`,\n  `BOUNDARY_REVIEWED` (per-reviewer outcome rows with #140 statuses) and\n  `REVIEW_ADJUDICATED` events carry rounds and pair outcomes. The reporting\n  projection (`performance/workflow-projection.js`) only needs to copy\n  bounded, enumerated values from these.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) project from the existing records in the reporting\n  projection; (b) add new journal events for metrics.\n- **Reversibility:** high; the projection is derived, replaceable reporting\n  memory.\n- **Decision:** (a). No protocol event or result shape changes. The\n  projection stays in the performance module, away from the files the\n  parallel #142/#143/#144 work edits.","file":"interview.md","heading":"D1 - Where the new fields come from"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** How is a demoted finding identified from the store?\n- **Answer:** A finding is demoted when the reviewer marked it blocking but\n  the round schedule did not let it block when it was raised: severity low\n  (low never blocks), or rounds 4-5 where only high findings and medium\n  regressions block. The projection computes the effective flag with the\n  same `scheduledBlocking` rule the boundary uses, from the result's own\n  `roundPolicy` (round and regressionPaths).\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) derive with `scheduledBlocking` from the recorded round;\n  (b) count only low findings; (c) wait for follow-up records (#148).\n- **Reversibility:** high.\n- **Decision:** (a). Each finding row carries `reviewerBlocking` (the\n  reviewer's flag), `blocking` (effective at raise time) and `demoted`.\n  Later re-evaluation of a prior finding against history (origin tracking) is\n  not replayed; the raise-time view is the measure.","file":"interview.md","heading":"D2 - Effective blocking and \"demoted\""},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** D6 measure 2 needs follow-up records, which #148 adds later.\n  What does this PR report?\n- **Answer:** The count of demoted findings by severity, with the failure\n  scenario recorded per finding (a boolean `hasFailureScenario`, never the\n  text), and the follow-up count explicitly reported as not recorded. The\n  measure's `met` value is `null` (not measurable) until follow-up rows exist.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) report demoted findings and mark follow-ups not recorded;\n  (b) invent a placeholder follow-up record; (c) implement #148 here.\n- **Reversibility:** high; #148 adds a follow-up field to the finding row and\n  the measure starts counting it.\n- **Decision:** (a). #148 is out of scope (separate issue, later wave).","file":"interview.md","heading":"D3 - Follow-up status before follow-up records exist"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** How does the store link an escaped defect to a demoted\n  finding?\n- **Answer:** Escaped-defect notes already take free-form origin `links`\n  with a human basis. Add one documented link form,\n  `finding:<result-hash>:<finding-id>`, naming the result that raised the\n  finding. The measure counts confirmed escaped defects with at least one such\n  link that matches a demoted finding row (by result reference and finding\n  ID). Result hashes are globally unique, so the join works across runs and\n  imported snapshots.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) `finding:<result-hash>:<finding-id>` links; (b) link to a\n  run and treat any demoted finding of it as the origin; (c) wait for\n  follow-up IDs (#148).\n- **Reversibility:** high; #148 can add a follow-up link form alongside it.\n- **Decision:** (a).","file":"interview.md","heading":"D4 - Escaped defects traced to demoted findings"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** D6 measure 4 names \"the second reviewer\". The paired\n  selection has no first/second order.\n- **Answer:** The concern was the cross-provider second opinion going\n  missing. Report the UNAVAILABLE rate and own findings per reviewer provider\n  (and model), over each paired round's final per-reviewer outcome\n  (`BOUNDARY_REVIEWED` rows, so repair and transient retries are not double\n  counted). The measure is met when every provider that took part is below\n  10% and produced at least one finding the peer did not report in that round\n  (by class ID).\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) per provider, met when all providers qualify; (b) treat the\n  non-implementing provider as second (needs the implementer's provider,\n  which run.start does not record reliably); (c) the provider with the higher\n  rate.\n- **Reversibility:** high; a report-time rule.\n- **Decision:** (a). It is stricter than the original wording and needs no\n  ordering.","file":"interview.md","heading":"D5 - Which reviewer is \"the second reviewer\""},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** How are rounds to PASS and \"a waive after a FAIL streak\"\n  computed?\n- **Answer:** Per workflow and review scope: the round of the first paired\n  round (`BOUNDARY_REVIEWED`) in which every reviewer completed with PASS, or\n  of a `REVIEW_ADJUDICATED` pair. Scopes with rounds but no PASS are reported\n  as open. A waive after a FAIL streak is a `waive` decision naming the\n  `review` gate recorded in a workflow whose latest paired round before it had\n  a FAIL and that scope never passed. The waiver's gate list is projected\n  (enumerated gate IDs only).\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) paired-round based; (b) count individual results.\n- **Reversibility:** high.\n- **Decision:** (a). Planning scopes are included as their own scopes when\n  they record rounds; the measure is reported over boundary scopes (`slice`,\n  `feature-final`), which is what D6 discussed.","file":"interview.md","heading":"D6 - Rounds to PASS and waives after a FAIL streak"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** D17 lists class ID and class statement per finding. The\n  projection rule so far is \"enumerated values and counts only, no\n  conversation text\".\n- **Answer:** Project `classId` (a reviewer slug) and `criterion` (a rubric\n  ID) as labels; project `classStatement` only when it is a single line of at\n  most 200 characters, otherwise omit it. Never project the failure scenario,\n  evidence or path text.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) as stated; (b) no class statement at all; (c) everything\n  D17 lists including scenario text.\n- **Reversibility:** medium; projected text reaches snapshots that may be\n  exported. Narrowing later needs a reprojection.\n- **Decision:** (a). The class statement is a one-line defect class name the\n  human approved in D17; scenario text stays in the run journal.","file":"interview.md","heading":"D7 - Text in the reporting store"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** Runs that were projected by rc.34 lack the new fields.\n- **Answer:** Version the workflow projection. A workflow whose stored\n  projection version is older is reprojected from its first event the next\n  time it is projected. Observation IDs are stable, so reprojection replaces\n  rows (new version, same ID) rather than duplicating them. Runs that are\n  never touched again keep their old rows and simply lack the fields; reports\n  treat missing fields as not recorded.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) projection version with reprojection; (b) a one-off repair\n  command over all local stores; (c) forward only.\n- **Reversibility:** high.\n- **Decision:** (a).","file":"interview.md","heading":"D8 - Rows already projected before this change"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** What is \"CLI status\" for these metrics?\n- **Answer:** A new `gatereeve metrics convergence` command reports the four\n  measures and the per-reviewer table, from the local reporting store by\n  default or from a fixed `--dataset`, as JSON or Markdown. The reevaluation\n  report's `measurement` gains the same `convergence` section so fleet\n  datasets show it too. `gatereeve status` already shows review scopes and\n  rounds (source AC11), so it is unchanged.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) new `metrics convergence`; (b) extend `metrics status`\n  (store health; it accepts no arguments); (c) extend protocol `status`.\n- **Reversibility:** high.\n- **Decision:** (a), plus the reevaluation section.","file":"interview.md","heading":"D9 - CLI surface"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** How large is the desktop part?\n- **Answer:** Small. The desktop metrics card already calls the shared\n  `metricsRequest` over IPC and embeds the reevaluation HTML. Add the\n  `convergence` action to the IPC allowlist (scoped to the selected project\n  like `report`), a \"Load convergence measures\" button and a convergence\n  section in the reevaluation HTML. The desktop mirror of the shared\n  resources is restaged with the existing sync script.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** (a) deliver it here; (b) leave it open with a comment on #149.\n- **Reversibility:** high.\n- **Decision:** (a).","file":"interview.md","heading":"D10 - Desktop surface"},{"answeredBy":"agent","body":"- **Question:** Fold in #136 (earlier-contract planning PASS qualification) or\n  the parked `metrics purge-test-data --workflows-file` item?\n- **Answer:** #136 is a planning-qualification fix in `delegation.js`, not a\n  metrics change, and does not fall out of this work. The purge command with\n  `--workflows-file` already exists on `main`; the parked item is an\n  operation on a live remote store, which this run must not touch.\n- **Answered by:** agent\n- **Options:** fold in / leave.\n- **Reversibility:** high.\n- **Decision:** Leave both. Say so in the PR.","file":"interview.md","heading":"D11 - Issue #136 and the purge parked item"}],"rule":"This is a goal run: the human was not asked. Assess every supplied agent-answered decision entry against the fixed mandate and the approved requirements. An entry that contradicts the mandate, exceeds its scope or makes an irreversible choice the human would need to make is blocking."},"artifact":"design","contract":"gatereeve/current/8","documents":{"design.md":{"bytes":5986,"hash":"sha256:830a0914329ff56bbb715ed85f6e3639a34382fb6dda78ffaf2924c33fbb6274","path":"design.md"},"interview.md":{"bytes":11281,"hash":"sha256:de8b2c52b44aa9ca105dfffa950c2eb769d6f5ccc22265e6c745878e315fe897","path":"interview.md"}},"evaluator":{"contextId":"01a21be6-bb5f-7f62-a910-2603705666ce","freshContext":true,"inheritedTurns":0,"model":"gpt-6-sol","provider":"codex","reasoningEffort":"high"},"featureId":"tb-metrics-remainder","findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"INCOMPLETE_D6_MEASURE","classStatement":"The proposed scope leaves a mandated success measure uncomputable.","document":"requirements/design.md","evidence":"Lines 60-62 specify follow-ups as “not recorded” and D6.2 met as null. Lines 121-124 exclude #148 follow-up records. The supporting D6 definition in requirements/interview.md:33-34 requires each demoted finding to be recorded as a follow-up with severity and failure scenario and decided at Completion.","failureScenario":"A finding is demoted -> the store has no follow-up or Completion decision for it -> the required D6.2 measure remains unmeasurable, so the PR cannot deliver all four mandated measures.","id":"F1","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"MISSING_FINDING_JOIN_KEY","classStatement":"The finding projection does not specify the key required to trace escaped defects.","document":"requirements/design.md","evidence":"Lines 34-38 list the projected finding fields without a result hash, while lines 63-64 require a join on result hash and finding ID. Lines 12-14 describe existing finding rows as holding only kind and finding ID; line 44 specifies a result-hash reference only for boundary-reviewer rows.","failureScenario":"An escaped-defect note links to a demoted finding by result hash and finding ID -> the finding observation has no specified result hash to join on -> the traced defect is omitted from D6.3.","id":"F2","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"INCOMPLETE_COHORT_SUCCESS","classStatement":"Measures can report success while older projected workflows are excluded.","document":"requirements/design.md","evidence":"Lines 51-52 reproject older workflows only the next time each is projected. Lines 71-72 and 113-114 acknowledge that untouched older rows lack fields, but lines 57-59 and 65-67 still allow measures to report met from the available subset.","failureScenario":"Older workflows with failures remain untouched while a newer workflow passes -> the report computes met from the newer rows despite incomplete historical coverage -> it reports success for a cohort whose required data are missing.","id":"F3","severity":"high"}],"kind":"planning-review","mandate":{"constraints":["Do not merge the PR.","Full rigor.","If the desktop surface turns out much larger than the CLI and metrics work, deliver metrics, CLI status and the user guide and leave the desktop part open with a comment.","Stay out of the files of the parallel #142, #143 and #144 work where possible; keep any needed edit there small.","Do not touch any live remote metrics store.","No local paths or other projects names in public issue or PR text.","Record genuinely open choices in the decision log and call them out in the PR description."],"goal":"One ready, unmerged PR that closes GitHub issue #149 (AC11 metrics remainder and surfaces: per-finding and per-reviewer metrics fields, the four D6 measures computed from the metrics store alone, CLI status and desktop surfaces, user guide), using the follow-up-feature doc as design input."},"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The mandate requires all four D6 measures computed from the metrics store alone. requirements/design.md:60-62 leaves D6.2 follow-ups unrecorded and its met value null; requirements/interview.md:30-34 says that measure includes recording demoted findings as follow-ups and deciding them at Completion.","outcome":"FAIL"},"outcome":"FAIL","output":{"bytes":2793,"format":"json","hash":"sha256:657e7eee7070c61fc2f1a38d746d59016b1ec42b751eba3058c1636b2d66f5eb"},"receipt":{"bytes":1362,"format":"json","hash":"sha256:9ca99cc7282e3d3bbf5e9d7e357da6152558db0a4050d75e1301952a196a3e42"},"reviewContract":"sha256:33046a7b328e55cf539c21c18523876347b7f41d2434ad14c6d2017a4fe115ee","runId":"d8a93770-a089-49d6-bd06-05022bed3e66","subject":"sha256:830a0914329ff56bbb715ed85f6e3639a34382fb6dda78ffaf2924c33fbb6274","summary":"The design states a real problem and bounds most of the work, but it cannot yet deliver the mandated four measures. Its finding join and treatment of older projections also allow incomplete data to be reported as success."}